   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law, in relation to expanding the duties of the women veterans coordinator",
    "basePrintNo": "S5432",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5432-2011",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §361-b, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5432\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the executive law, in relation to expanding the duties of the\nwomen veterans coordinator\n\nPURPOSE:\nThe purpose of this bill is to clarify and update the duties of the\nwomen veterans coordinator within the New York State Division of\nVeterans' Affairs.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nSection One - Subdivision 1 of this bill amends Section 361-b of the\nExecutive Law to clarify certain points relating to the duties of the\nWomen Veterans Coordinator. This includes deleting certain\nresponsibilities involved with the state veterans nursing homes. The\nfollowing functions are added to the position of the Women Veterans\nCoordinator making recommendations to the director regarding the\nimprovement of benefits and services to women veterans; being the\nliaison between the division and the United States department of\nveterans affairs center for women veterans and military\norganizations; promoting events and activities that recognize,\neducate and honor women veterans; adding a description of the women\nveterans coordinators activities for the calendar year and the\nprograms developed in the annual report to the director and such\ninformation to be included in the directors annual report to the\ngovernor and the Legislature.\n\nSection Two - This act shall take effect immediately.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nChapter 271 of the Laws of 1994 and Chapter 358 of the Laws of 1999\nwere written and passed in order to ensure that women veterans have\nequal access to the Department of Veterans Affairs facilities by\nrequiring the appointment of a women veterans coordinator to serve as\nan advocate for women veterans.\n\nAt the time of the enactment of the original chapter, the legislation\nwas drafted to model the duties of the women veterans coordinator\nposition established within each Department of Veterans Affairs\nmedical centers. Since that time, other states including Indiana,\nKentucky, Minnesota, Missouri and Texas have created a Women Veterans\nCoordinator within their state agencies dedicated to military\nveterans. This proposal removes specific duties on the state level\nthat are the responsibilities of those Women veterans coordinators at\neach of the federal Department of Veterans Affairs medical centers\nand adds functions that are more reflected of the statewide mission\nof the New York State Division of Veterans' Affairs.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew Legislation.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nTo be determined.\n\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
